<</Type/Catalog/Pages 1 0 R/Metadata 574 0 R/Lang(en)/StructTreeRoot 26 0 R/MarkInfo<</Marked true/Suspects false>>/ViewerPreferences<</Direction/L2R>>/Outlines 25 0 R/Names<</Dests<</Names[(1-problem-essence)474 0 R(2-assumptions-table)475 0 R(3-ground-truths)476 0 R(4-derivation-chains)477 0 R(5-abandoned-reasoning)489 0 R(6-conclusion)494 0 R(60000-dollars-pay-down-the-mortgage-or-invest)472 0 R(conclusion-c1-option-a-delivers-a-guaranteed-riskless-fully-after-tax-nominal-return-of-625-annually-for-as-long-as-the-loan-remains-outstanding)478 0 R(conclusion-c10-applying-the-full-60000-to-mortgage-principal-option-a-wins-a-weighted-trade-off-against-option-b-a-5050-split-and-simply-holding-the-60000-as-cash-and-the-win-is-robust-to-any-single-criterion-reweighting-smaller-than-a-3-point-swing)487 0 R(conclusion-c11-the-recommended-action-is-to-apply-the-full-60000-to-mortgage-principal-via-a-formal-recast-while-separately-verifying-and-maximizing-any-currently-unused-401kirahsa-room-using-ongoing-cash-flow)488 0 R(conclusion-c2-option-bs-after-tax-10-year-cagr-net-of-dividend-drag-and-exit-capital-gains-tax-plausibly-ranges-from-about-34-to-about-90-with-roughly-34-51-as-the-valuation-conditioned-base-case-band)479 0 R(conclusion-c3-the-current-historically-elevated-starting-valuation-makes-the-vanguard-forward-looking-range-not-the-unconditional-historical-average-the-more-defensible-central-planning-estimate-for-this-specific-10-year-window)480 0 R(conclusion-c4-option-b-only-matches-option-as-guaranteed-hurdle-if-realized-10-year-pretax-nominal-equity-returns-exceed-approximately-75-annually--above-the-current-forward-looking-forecast-and-below-the-unconditional-historical-average)481 0 R(conclusion-c5-no-investment-grade-fixed-income-or-cash-alternative-available-today-can-match-option-as-guaranteed-hurdle-so-the-live-choice-is-specifically-between-option-a-and-equities-not-between-option-a-and-safe-alternatives)482 0 R(conclusion-c6-option-b-adds-leverage-like-correlated-balance-sheet-risk-that-option-a-removes-through-the-actions-of-other-parties-lenders-and-employers-in-a-downturn-not-merely-through-market-variance-itself)483 0 R(conclusion-c7-converting-cash-to-home-equity-via-extra-principal-is-far-less-reversible-than-converting-it-to-brokerage-shares-a-real-option-value-the-return-comparison-in-c1-c4-does-not-capture)484 0 R(conclusion-c8-prepaying-the-mortgage-early-forfeits-part-of-the-inflation-hedge-a-fixed-nominal-27-year-liability-otherwise-provides-a-benefit-that-is-small-immediately-but-compounds-over-the-horizon)485 0 R(conclusion-c9-any-currently-unused-tax-advantaged-retirement-or-hsa-space-strictly-dominates-taxable-brokerage-investing-for-new-dollars-independent-of-how-the-60000-itself-is-allocated-between-option-a-and-option-b)486 0 R(dead-end-comparing-option-as-hurdle-against-a-single-point-estimate-equity-return-instead-of-a-bracket)490 0 R(dead-end-recommending-option-a-on-the-general-behavioral-finance-platitude-that-debt-payoff-is-always-the-psychologically-safer-choice)492 0 R(dead-end-treating-recast-vs-plain-extra-payment-as-an-immaterial-implementation-detail)493 0 R(dead-end-using-the-unconditional-historical-105-average-as-the-sole-forecast-for-option-b)491 0 R(executive-summary)473 0 R]>>>>>>
